# @epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone — the DECLARATIVE HALF
# of the four-conjunct invariant at ouroboros altitude. Property
# shard that carries the four sub-predicates + one composed
# bilateral the @kintsugi/ouroboros species-decl (Mara-A `9eb0898`)
# named as its Mara-composable companion landing per §4.5.4.
#
# Arc-1 Tick 1.5 Landing 7 companion per docs/specs/kintsugi-
# ouroboros-compiler-self-collapse.md §8.1 Landing 7. The species-
# decl side landed at `shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror` (Mara-A
# 2026-07-15, 576 LOC); this property shard lands alongside per
# §4.5.4 four-sub-predicate + one-composed-bilateral decomposition.
#
# === Forward-promise discharge ===
#
# The species-decl at `shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror:479-524`
# named ouroboros_monotone as the load-bearing bilateral AND
# forward-promised sub-predicate decomposition at "companion
# property shard `@epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone`"
# (line 500). This shard IS the discharge. The composed bilateral
# on the species-decl side (line 524) composes via `requires` over
# the four sub-predicates declared here.
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; seventh instance at
# @epistemologic/property altitude) ===
#
# Sibling species at @epistemologic/property/*:
#
#   cold_compile_within_tolerance    (Tick 43; 2026-06-20)
#   dark_count_monotone              (Tick 41; 2026-06-19)
#   restart_intensity_well_formed    (2026-07-03; fourth #53)
#   docblock_grounded                (Trio slot 1; 2026-07-06)
#   docblock_coherent                (Trio slot 2; 2026-07-06)
#   docblock_no_extraction_pattern   (Trio slot 3; 2026-07-06)
#   verdict_is_content_addressed     (N1 Tick 1; 2026-07-12)
#   ouroboros_monotone               (THIS; Arc-1 Tick 1.5 Landing 7)
#
# The bilateral discipline per Recognition #53
# (`[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`): declarative
# property at `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational
# fracture body at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by
# the kintsugi loop. The paired fracture at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/ouroboros_monotone` is forward-promised per
# §4.5.6 companion (composes from
# `@kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone` 2026-07-01 +
# `@kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance` 2026-07-04
# templates).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word + ancestry chain ===
#
# The word `monotone` appears in 10+ landed shards prior; two-tick
# discipline picks `ouroboros_monotone` (matches species-decl's
# naming; preserves the substrate's `ouroboros` vocabulary). Load-
# bearing ancestor sites:
#
#   shards/mirror/bench.mirror:40-54 + :363
#     THREE-CONJUNCT template `monotone_non_increasing(op, n, np1,
#     tolerance) -> verdict` (runtime ≤ (1+tolerance) × runtime ∧
#     output ≡ ∧ env ≡). The extension-by-one-axis composition-
#     honest ancestor.
#   shards/epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#     Tick 41; first ouroboros bite; single-conjunct precedent.
#   shards/epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_tolerance
#     .mirror  Tick 43; second bite; three-conjunct specialisation.
#   shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror:479-524  (Mara-A `9eb0898`)
#     Species-decl side of the composed bilateral this shard's
#     four sub-predicates satisfy; named this shard as forward-
#     promise at :500.
#   docs/specs/kintsugi-ouroboros-compiler-self-collapse.md
#     (Mara-B canonical) §4.5 four-conjunct math + §5.3
#     composition + §7.7 A7 four-sub-predicate landing sequence.
#   docs/scouts/2026-07-15-taut-kintsugi-ouroboros-substrate-
#     scout.md  Taut #108 §D4 grep-first ratification + §E A7.
#   Companion fracture templates (§4.5.6):
#     shards/kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#       (Tick 41; single-conjunct fracture body).
#     shards/kintsugi/fracture/cold_compile_within_tolerance.mirror
#       (Tick 43; three-conjunct fracture body).
#
# === The four conjuncts per §4.5.2 ===
#
# The composed bilateral (species-decl side + property-side
# carrier below) expands to:
#
#   ouroboros_monotone(before, after) ⇔
#       rust_LOC(after)                  ≤ rust_LOC(before)
#     ∧ test_pass_rate(after)            ≥ test_pass_rate(before)
#     ∧ io_violations(after)             ≤ io_violations(before)
#     ∧ sbec(after)                      ≥ sbec(before)
#
# The four conjuncts extend @mirror/bench.monotone_non_increasing's
# three-conjunct template (runtime + output + env) by adding the
# `sbec` conjunct — the shard-body-executable-coverage fraction the
# Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR + Arc-2..N per-file collapses drive from 0
# to ≥ epsilon over the arc.
#
# Substrate-honest reuse per §4.5.3: the arc does NOT invent new
# invariant machinery. The three-conjunct template stays intact;
# ouroboros altitude adds ONE axis specific to the arc's concern
# (executable coverage of shard bodies through the evaluator). The
# extension is composition, not replacement.
#
# === Sub-predicate + composed-bilateral decomposition per §4.5.4 ===
#
# The four-conjunct lands as FOUR sub-predicates + ONE composed
# bilateral (matches StageFreight `stagefreight_addressable`
# substrate-decl pattern per Seam tick 68 C4/C9 closure). Each
# sub-predicate is a first-class substrate object; the composed
# bilateral is not opaque — Arc-2..N ticks may consume any single
# sub-predicate as its own admissibility gate without paying the
# full four-conjunct cost when the tick's concern is narrower.
#
# The composed bilateral on THIS property side (below) is the
# same shape as the one on the species-decl side (line 524 of
# `shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror`); on the property side it
# lives as first-class substrate carrier that Arc-2..N ticks
# CONSUME during collapse ratification. Two altitudes; one
# invariant; consumption via species-decl for tick-level
# admissibility and via property carrier for cache-keyable
# admissibility discipline.
#
# === Rice-safe per §4.5.5 ===
#
# The four conjuncts are Rice-safe because none of them requires
# halting-problem-hard analysis:
#
#   rust_loc_non_increasing         line-count over
#                                    bootstrap/src/*.rs (empirical
#                                    ratchet; syntactic; O(n) walk).
#   test_pass_rate_non_decreasing   fraction of green tests
#                                    (empirical crystal presence
#                                    via @mirror/store).
#   io_violations_non_increasing    count of shard actions reaching
#                                    non-@io surfaces (syntactic
#                                    membership check via
#                                    @io/algebra).
#   sbec_non_decreasing             fraction of substrate-decl'd
#                                    action bodies the evaluator
#                                    can dispatch (empirical
#                                    evaluator surface enumeration).
#
# The invariant checks empirical crystal state, not program
# semantics. Individual shard bodies may compute Turing-complete
# computations; the invariant does not read program semantics —
# only the tick-boundary metric state. This is a load-bearing
# bound the arc must preserve at every tick.
#
# === Composes with @autopoietic + @torus (via species-decl) ===
#
# This property shard declares the invariant only. The species-
# decl side at `shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror` composes the
# invariant with `@autopoietic.autopoietic_closure_holds` +
# `@torus.autonomy(compiler, ouroboros_winding)` in the
# `collapse_admissible` bilateral (line 477). The three-gate
# admissibility discipline lives at the species-decl; this
# property shard supplies the four-conjunct invariant that is
# the first of the three gates.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   monotone ranking functions  Floyd-Hoare-Dijkstra well-founded
#                                orders; each sub-predicate IS a
#                                ranking function over one axis; the
#                                composed bilateral IS lexicographic.
#   Bencher / Criterion.rs      three-conjunct threshold discipline
#                                @mirror/bench extends and this
#                                shard extends by one axis.
#   Bazel REAPI ActionCache     content-addressed verdict caching
#                                per @epistemologic/property/
#                                verdict_is_content_addressed
#                                (N1 Tick 1) — the composed bilateral
#                                is cache-keyable by construction.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
# - Sub-predicates take `metric` per spec §4.5.4 signature; the
#   composed bilateral takes `ouroboros_state`. Field-to-metric
#   lowering (`rust_loc: int` -> `metric`, `test_pass_rate: float`
#   -> `metric`, etc.) lives at the species-decl side's `requires`
#   clauses per §4.5.4 landing sequence.
# - All four sub-predicate bodies obligation-blocked (`\`). Arc-1
#   evaluator FLOOR (Ticks 1.1-1.4) lifts the dispatch threshold;
#   Arc-2 Tick 2.1 empirically discharges first bodies (on the
#   spectral_signature.rs collapse per Reed migration-map §6).
# - Paired fracture `@kintsugi/fracture/ouroboros_monotone`
#   (§4.5.6 companion) forward-promised as Landing 7 sibling.
#   Composes from two prior fracture templates.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53; seventh instance at
#                       @epistemologic/property altitude),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]]
#                       (#87; composition-honest ancestor),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (@epistemologic = form-side; paired fracture
#                       at @kintsugi = process-side),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (`monotone` + `ouroboros` prior sites
#                       decisive per two-tick discipline),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (`metric`,
#                       `ouroboros_state`, `ouroboros_bench_pair`
#                       are typed carriers),
#                      [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]]
#                       (pure substrate-decl; NO Rust; discharges
#                       §7.7 A7 companion property landing),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (declarative
#                       half lands here; operational fracture
#                       @kintsugi/fracture/ouroboros_monotone at
#                       Landing 7 sibling; bodies discharge Arc-2..N).
# Related shards: kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror (species-decl; composed
#                  bilateral at :479-524 requires the four sub-
#                  predicates minted here),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (three-conjunct template
#                  ancestor at :40-54 + :363),
#                 epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (first ouroboros bite; single-conjunct precedent),
#                 epistemologic/property/cold_compile_within_
#                  tolerance.mirror (second bite; three-conjunct
#                  specialisation precedent),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/ouroboros_monotone.mirror
#                  (OPERATIONAL HALF; forward-promised Landing 7).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/programming/bencher-criterion-2014

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @mirror/bench
in @kintsugi/ouroboros

prism @epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone {
  focus ouroboros_monotone
  project ouroboros_monotone
  split ouroboros_monotone
  shift ouroboros_monotone
  settle ouroboros_monotone
}

# === Type carriers ===

# ouroboros_bench_pair — paired bench_crystal snapshot at two
# adjacent arc ticks.
#
# Derived from @mirror/bench.bench_crystal: `before` is the
# tick-n measurement; `after` is the tick-(n+1) measurement. The
# pair IS the substrate object Arc-2..N ticks compose over when
# they consume the composed ouroboros_monotone bilateral for
# cache-keyable admissibility per @epistemologic/property/
# verdict_is_content_addressed (N1 Tick 1; 2026-07-12).
#
# The composed bilateral's cache key is (spec_oid, target_oid,
# inputs_oid) per verdict_is_content_addressed; the inputs_oid
# lifts from the ouroboros_bench_pair's byte-content — same pair
# -> same input hash -> same verdict, always. Content-addressed
# verdict caching at the ouroboros altitude discharges via this
# carrier.
#
# before  bench_crystal at tick n. Records op = ouroboros_step,
#          args_oid = ouroboros_state hash at tick n, runtime_ns =
#          tick n step time, output_oid = ouroboros_state hash at
#          tick n+1 (the step's output), env_oid = arc environment
#          fingerprint (bootstrap toolchain + arc phase), tick_index
#          = n.
# after   bench_crystal at tick n+1. Same shape; predecessor field
#          links back to `before`; tick_index = n+1.
#
# Identity contract: two ouroboros_bench_pairs are equal iff
# `before` and `after` are bench_crystal-equal per @mirror/bench's
# septuple byte-equality contract.
type ouroboros_bench_pair = {
  before: bench_crystal,
  after:  bench_crystal,
}

# === Sub-predicates per §4.5.4 ===
#
# Four first-class bilaterals; each is a substrate object Arc-2..N
# ticks may consume independently when the tick's concern is
# narrower than the full four-conjunct. All bodies obligation-
# blocked (`\`); discharge via Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR (Tick 1.1-1.4)
# + Arc-2..N per-file empirical fires (first empirical fire at
# Arc-2 Tick 2.1 on spectral_signature.rs per Reed migration-map
# §6).
#
# Shared verdict semantics (per @glass `verdict` surface):
#   pass                — the tick's axis discharges (comparison
#                          holds strictly or with equality).
#   partial(confidence) — the axis regresses by a bounded noise/
#                          flake/deferred-resolution delta;
#                          confidence carries the delta magnitude
#                          (per @kintsugi/consent.query_phi
#                          re-verify discipline).
#   failure(reason)     — the axis regresses beyond the noise
#                          floor; reason carries the specific
#                          axis-violation narrative.
#
# The four per-axis rationales:

# rust_loc_non_increasing — first conjunct. Empirical ratchet on
# rust_LOC across bootstrap/src/*.rs; the arc forecloses Rust
# growth. Each admissible tick either deletes LOC or leaves it
# unchanged (structurally-independent-file case).
rust_loc_non_increasing(before: metric, after: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# test_pass_rate_non_decreasing — second conjunct. Substrate
# collapses green by MOVING green from Rust-hosted to shard-body-
# hosted, not by breaking green: pass rate must ascend (or hold)
# across every admissible tick.
test_pass_rate_non_decreasing(before: metric, after: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# io_violations_non_increasing — third conjunct. Count of shard
# actions reaching non-@io surfaces; each collapse must preserve
# or reduce it. Composition-only discipline per
# [substrate-floor:@io-boundary] marker: new BUSINESS_LOGIC shard
# bodies MUST compose only over @io + Arc-1-dispatched combinators.
io_violations_non_increasing(before: metric, after: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# sbec_non_decreasing — fourth conjunct; the NEW AXIS at ouroboros
# altitude that @mirror/bench's three-conjunct template does not
# carry. Fraction of substrate-decl'd action bodies the evaluator
# can dispatch. Initial value at Arc-1 landing = 0; Arc-1 Ticks
# 1.1-1.4 lift to > 0 via evaluator FLOOR combinator surface;
# Arc-2..N per-file collapses drive sbec toward 1. The arc's
# whole point IS lifting sbec across ticks.
sbec_non_decreasing(before: metric, after: metric) -> verdict { \ }

# === Composed bilateral per §4.5.4 ===
#
# ouroboros_monotone — LOAD-BEARING at substrate altitude. Same
# shape as the composed bilateral on the species-decl side at
# `shards/kintsugi/ouroboros.mirror:524`; on the property side
# it lives as first-class carrier that Arc-2..N ticks CONSUME
# during collapse ratification.
#
# Two altitudes; one invariant:
#   Species-decl side  the arc's per-tick admissibility gate
#                       composed inside `collapse_admissible` at
#                       :477 alongside `@autopoietic.autopoietic_
#                       closure_holds` + `@torus.autonomy(compiler,
#                       ouroboros_winding)`.
#   Property side      the cache-keyable admissibility discipline:
#                       Arc-2..N ticks consume this bilateral,
#                       memoize the verdict per (spec_oid,
#                       target_oid, inputs_oid) triple per
#                       @epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_
#                       addressed, and skip re-verification when
#                       the input triple has not changed.
#
# Composition is not opaque: each of the four `requires` clauses
# names a first-class sub-predicate declared above; the composed
# bilateral discharges iff all four sub-predicates discharge.
# Verdict shape matches the sub-predicates (pass / partial /
# failure); partial iff exactly one sub-predicate is partial;
# failure iff one or more sub-predicates fail.
#
# Body obligation-blocked; discharges cumulatively across Arc-2..N
# as the four sub-predicate bodies land empirical fires.
ouroboros_monotone(before: ouroboros_state, after: ouroboros_state) -> verdict
  requires rust_loc_non_increasing(before.rust_loc, after.rust_loc)
  requires test_pass_rate_non_decreasing(before.test_pass_rate, after.test_pass_rate)
  requires io_violations_non_increasing(before.io_violations, after.io_violations)
  requires sbec_non_decreasing(before.sbec, after.sbec)
{ \ }

# === Exports ===

out @epistemologic/property/ouroboros_monotone
out ouroboros_bench_pair
out rust_loc_non_increasing
out test_pass_rate_non_decreasing
out io_violations_non_increasing
out sbec_non_decreasing
out ouroboros_monotone
